\[\frac{1}{\beta}=\frac{c\Delta t}{s} \tag{3.4}\]

where, \(c\) is the speed of light and \(s\) total path length measure by TPC. The particle mass, \(M\) calculated by the associated momentum and inverse velocity via,

\[M=p\sqrt{(\frac{1}{\beta})^{2}-1} \tag{3.5}\]

TOF has 100 \(ps\) of time interval resolution. The combination of TPC and TOF made STAR a powerful particle identifier. The PID capability of STAR using TOF is shown in the Figure 3.11[96].

