One of the most important part of this analysis is the track quality. In heavy ion collision like RHIC, there are thousand of tracks coming from the collision center. All tracks that we detect in the detectors are not coming from the fireball and hence they are not 100% pure event tracks. The main impurity comes from the secondary particles, not produced in the collision and comes from the secondary reactions. These secondary particle or tracks comes from the reaction with the detector material and scattering effects etc. this making it imperative to check the track quality.

